# Server-only secrets — store in Supabase Dashboard → Edge Functions → Secrets
# (and/or EAS Secrets for build-time needs). Never commit values.
#
# Required by Edge Functions (send-push, delete-account):
#   SERVICE_ROLE_KEY          (or SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY)
#   SUPABASE_URL              (usually auto-injected)
#   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY         (usually auto-injected)
#   FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID
#   FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL
#   FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY
#
# Auth emails (signup confirmation / OTP) are NOT Edge Function secrets.
# Configure Custom SMTP in the Dashboard:
#   Authentication → Sign In / Emails → SMTP Settings
# Without working Custom SMTP, signup fails with:
#   "Error sending confirmation email"
#
# Optional (bot / ops / contact):
#   TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN
#   ADMIN_CHAT_ID
#   RESEND_API_KEY            (preferred email delivery for contact form)
#   CONTACT_EMAIL_TO          (default: designerphonex@gmail.com)
#   CONTACT_EMAIL_FROM        (Resend verified sender, e.g. Phoenix Print <onboarding@resend.dev>)
#
# Contact Edge Function: supabase/functions/contact
# Deploy: npx supabase functions deploy contact --project-ref jyoqmpfwkzejnzwhhkpx
# Without RESEND_API_KEY the function uses FormSubmit.co → CONTACT_EMAIL_TO
# (activate the destination inbox on first FormSubmit email if prompted).

# Database trigger vault (pg_net → send-push):
#   vault secret name: service_role_key
#
# After removing these from git history / local .env, rotate each key
# that was ever committed. See security hardening report.
